## Fix: Task 6 review round 2 (MERGE skip records the _data version; one-way history dependency)
================================================================================

Context: Review round 2 of Task 6. Only the app-managed Lakebase net apply
recorded `data_table_version`, so on the Delta engine (and on managed-synced
Lakebase and Neo4j) the MERGE skip's version check never applied: a build that
merged other content into `_data` and then failed before its apply was passed
over, and a later build whose mapping reverted to the base's could be skipped
while `_data`, the served graph, held the failed build's content. A failing
store probe in the skip check failed the build, and the last_build stamp's lazy
import made TwinBuildPostMaterialize and TwinBuildRunHistory depend on each
other.

Changes:

1. src/back/objects/digitaltwin/build/TwinMergeFallback.py
   After a successful MERGE the build records `data_table_version` and
   `data_table_id` of `_data` (None / "" when unreadable; the Lakebase net
   apply reads both again). A skipped build carries the base's version and
   table id forward. The skip compares the live table id with the base's
   when both have one, next to the version check. A store probe that raises
   reads as "no graph" (warning; the build merges instead of skipping).
2. src/back/objects/digitaltwin/build/TwinBuildRunHistory.py,
   src/back/objects/digitaltwin/build/TwinBuildPostMaterialize.py,
   src/back/objects/digitaltwin/build/_build_pipeline.py
   Move Method `persist_last_build_to_registry` into TwinBuildRunHistory; the
   pipeline hook calls it there. TwinBuildPostMaterialize no longer imports
   TwinBuildRunHistory.
3. Tests: tests/units/objects/test_build_pipeline_net_apply.py (the MERGE
   records the version and table id; Delta base merge@7 with `_data`@8 merges,
   @7 skips; another table id merges; the skip carries version and id forward;
   a failing store probe merges), and the delegation test in
   tests/units/objects/test_build_pipeline_compute_once.py
   (`TestPersistLastBuildHook::test_the_pipeline_delegates_to_the_collaborator`,
   now patching TwinBuildRunHistory).

Known limitations (deferred by review):
- Lakebase skip runs are passed over in the base search, so after 50
  consecutive skipped builds the base leaves the window and one full stream
  runs (safe, periodic).
- The empty-graph completion in `_apply_full_rebuild` keeps its own message
  and `build_mode: "full"`.

