## Fix: Task 8 review round 1 (reconciler counts like the MV, honest 404, DAB template)
================================================================================

Context: the Task 8 review found the reconciler reporting drift on healthy
graphs, a 404 that also covered outages, and a DAB template that did not match
the runner.

Changes:

1. src/back/core/helpers/SQLHelpers.py, src/back/core/graphdb/delta/MaterializedViewBuilder.py,
   src/back/core/streaming/SlotReconciler.py
   `NON_BLANK_OBJECT_SQL` (the `WHERE object IS NOT NULL AND TRIM(object) != ''`
   the `_data` MV applies to its slots branch) is now one constant; the
   reconciler applies it inside both DISTINCT totals and the per-`map_id`
   query, so `_slots` rows for unset attributes (blank objects kept as
   upserts) no longer read as drift. An unreadable count or a missing row is
   an `InfrastructureError`, not a zero (two garbled answers must not compare
   equal). Comment on the DECIMAL(38,0) cast made exact (BIGINT sums overflow
   after a handful of 64-bit hashes in ANSI mode).
2. src/back/objects/digitaltwin/build/TwinSlotReconciliation.py
   A missing warehouse client is an `InfrastructureError`; the slots table is
   looked up with `WarehouseStatements.query("SHOW TABLES IN … LIKE …")`
   (`slots_table_listed`), so a permission gap or an outage surfaces as
   502/503 instead of "no incremental build has run" (404 only for a clean
   empty listing). The mapping compile uses `DEFAULT_BASE_URI` like the main
   build.
3. src/api/routers/internal/dtwin.py
   The reconcile scans run on the build warehouse as the caller
   (`create_databricks_client(..., warehouse_id=resolve_build_warehouse_id(...))`
   keeps the OBO token; a Lakehouse//RT query warehouse would hit its
   guardrails).
4. resources/triple_slots.pipeline.yml.example
   Matches `SlotPipelineRunner.ensure`: pipeline name
   `ontobricks-slots-<domain>-v<n>`, a `file:` library pointing at the
   uploaded workspace SQL file, configuration key `ontobricks.slot_sql_sha256`,
   channel from `settings.slot_pipeline_channel`; warns against copying the
   block for an app-built domain (two pipelines would write one `_slots`).
   tests/units/settings/test_bundle_job_resource.py now uncomments the block
   and parses it as a pipeline resource.
5. docs/incremental-materialization.md
